Q1.Show Department with the highest number of employees.

SELECT deptno
FROM emp
GROUP BY deptno
HAVING COUNT(*) = (
    SELECT MAX(COUNT(*))
    FROM emp
    GROUP BY deptno
);

Q2. Show department name and the total salary of the employees in that department.

SELECT d.dname, SUM(e.sal) AS total_salary
FROM emp e
JOIN dept d ON e.deptno = d.deptno
GROUP BY d.dname;


Q3.Find Employees earning more than the average salary.

SELECT *
FROM emp
WHERE sal > (SELECT AVG(sal) FROM emp);


Q4. Show employees whose salary is greater than 'ALLEN'.

SELECT *
FROM emp
WHERE sal > (
    SELECT sal
    FROM emp
    WHERE ename = 'ALLEN'
);


Q5 . Display Department number, total Salary, and average commission.

